From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:25:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple-vxd: Add the stateless HEVC decoder

Expose V4L2_PIX_FMT_HEVC_SLICE next to H.264: frame-based decoding with
Annex-B start codes (what FFmpeg's v4l2request hwaccel, GStreamer's
v4l2slh265dec and libva-v4l2-request send), the SPS, PPS, SLICE_PARAMS,
SCALING_MATRIX and DECODE_PARAMS controls, NV12 output.

Per picture the unit locates the slice NALs in the OUTPUT buffer,
resolves the DPB to CAPTURE buffers by timestamp and runs the builder.
The slice header's length comes from data_byte_offset, which FFmpeg and
libva count from the buffer and GStreamer from the slice's start code;
both are accepted.  ENTRY_POINT_OFFSETS is not offered: the hardware
does not take them (the kext never reads them from its slice header).

Buffers follow CHEVCDecoder: per context the four Genc buffers sized
from the picture, the intra, aux-line and stream-state buffers and the
slice structure buffer; per CAPTURE buffer the temporal MVs, fragment
pointer table, above parameters and the record the co-located picture's
words are read back from.  The kext's 1 MiB slice parameter buffer per
picture is one per context here, as it is only read while its picture
decodes.

The unit registers only when the SoC's match data gives the HEVC
parameters, and not on core revision 0x70600 (S8000 A0/A1), which needs
AppleD5500's BRN50577 dummy-picture workaround.

Assisted-by: LLM
